    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. There are only 3 test files (`AcceptanceTest`, `AcceptanceBase`, and one other), and surefire runs the single `AcceptanceTest` which now passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `capacityWarning` flag so it returns `true` when an owner's city already holds between 40 and 49 owners (approaching the hard limit of 50), leaving the existing hard rejection at 50 unchanged.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a new `capacityWarning` boolean (readOnly) property to the `Owner` schema, as a sibling of the existing `bulkSignupWarning`. This regenerates `OwnerDto` with `getCapacityWarning`/`setCapacityWarning`.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**:\n   - Added a `CITY_CAPACITY_WARNING_THRESHOLD = 40` constant.\n   - Added `approachingCityCapacity(String city)` \u2014 counts owners in the city case-insensitively (same logic as the existing `requireCityBelowCapacity` hard check) and returns `true` when the count is `>= 40` and `< 50` (i.e. 40\u201349 inclusive).\n   - Wired it into `toOwnerDtoWithBulkWarning(...)` via `ownerDto.setCapacityWarning(...)`, so the flag is populated on every read/list/create response (matching how `bulkSignupWarning` works). Since it's computed on read, the acceptance test's flow (fill a city to 40, create the 41st owner, then GET it) correctly yields `capacityWarning: true`.\n\nThe hard rejection path (`requireCityBelowCapacity` throwing `CityAtCapacityException` at 50) is untouched.",
